+# Flight Logbook
+
+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.
+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.
+
+## 2026-09-02
+
+### 0330 — Canonical decode nesting depth capped at 256
+- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/canonicaljson/canonical.go:355` `decodeValue` recursed once per nesting level with no bound; a 2 MB document of one million nested arrays exhausted the goroutine stack and killed the process with an uncatchable `fatal error: stack overflow` at every public entry, well under the 5,242,880-byte identity size cap.
+- FIX: `MaxNestingDepth = 256` (`canonical.go:38`) enforced inside `decodeValue` before recursion, typed `ErrInvalidJSON`; inherited by `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity`, `VerifyObjectIdentity` through the shared `decodeStrict`.
+- FINDING: deepest pinned v0.5.0 closed shape (Transfer Manifest, 16-level submodule forest, 4-level extensions) decodes at depth 38, so 256 leaves over 6x headroom for normative objects.
+- DECISION: tests pin the bound from a test-local literal, not the constant; widen-257, widen-512, narrow-255 and delete-gate mutants all exit 1 (delete-gate reproduces the original stack overflow).
+- SCOPE: `internal/canonicaljson/canonical.go`, `internal/canonicaljson/nesting_depth_test.go`, `README.md:146`, `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/constraint-enumeration.md`.
+- STATUS: BUG-260902-lyhvkw handed to review; coverage 87.1% -> 87.2%, all configured gates exit 0.
